Go modules (go.mod, workers/ottl-0.163/go.mod, and workers/ottl-0.164/go.mod) and npm packages
(package-lock.json, pipeline-ui/package-lock.json)
are fetched at build time and stay under their own licenses. Those manifests are
the source-tree inventory. This repository does not vendor their source, and it
does not track built SPA bundles or collector binaries.

Container base images, the collector image, and the optional upstream
`ghcr.io/ctrlspice/otel-desktop-viewer:v0.7.0` image are pinned by digest in
Dockerfiles, Compose files, and Makefile. The desktop viewer is not built or
vendored here; its image and contents remain under upstream licenses.

Redistributing a built image or binary bundles those dependencies. Comply with
their upstream licenses. This source MIT grant is not that clearance.
